      "title": "Iceland rejects EU accession talks after divisive referendum campaign",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/30/iceland-eu-accession-talks-referendum-result",
      "description": "<p>Well-funded no camp prevails, winning 52.8% of votes and gaining plaudits from Eurosceptic figures across Europe</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/30/definitely-no-or-maybe-yes-what-tipped-the-icelandic-referendum\">Analysis: Definitely no or maybe yes – what tipped the Icelandic referendum</a></p></li></ul><p>Voters in Iceland have ⁠rejected ⁠a government proposal ​to reopen ⁠accession talks with ⁠the ​EU after a closely fought referendum campaign that divided the country against a backdrop of global volatility.</p><p>After a long and anxious night for those on both sides of the debate, the no camp ended up with 52.8% of votes on Sunday morning and the yes camp with 47.2%. Voter turnout was high at 82.5%.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/30/iceland-eu-accession-talks-referendum-result\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
